  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As the titles states - people who block you no longer are visible to you in ANY capacity as far as I can tell. If you block someone you also cannot see them in ANY capacity.\nThis means to get unblocked or unblock someone else you MUST use the website or search their name with the undeniably inaccurate and old search feature.\nWhy is this a problem?  First: Crashers will autoblock instance owners and start crashing people. This means the instance is repopulated as the players rejoin only for the crasher to visit again and crash everyone all over again. Repeat forever because nobody knows who joined and caused the crash or that it even was a crasher.\nReason #2: Sometimes people will jokingly block each other for varying reasons to be funny. This used to not be a problem because you could open the social list, select them, and then unblock them. Now it's a pain in the butt and not worth your time for a silly one-off joke.\nReason #3: You can now join a friend and think they are alone in a world - only to find out that they are with someone and you were just blocked by the other person. or maybe you blocked them. Previously, you could check the social menu and see if the person you joined was with anyone you blocked or who had blocked you. Now you can't. Why?\nThe only reason I can think of this change being made is because the VRC devs made the huge assumption that when you block someone you don't ever want to see them again - period. Never ever. not even on the social list. The very sight of their name/avatar is enough to make you freak out. This is not a good enough reason to expose users to endless public instance crasher bots, the annoyance of unblocking people now, and the realization/awkwardness of finding out there is another person in the room that you can't see in any way. The best part is - the other party gets the awkwardness too! Neither person knows the other is in the room until the mutual friend starts informing them!\nTL;DR - There are a myriad of reasons that you want to see who you have blocked/who has blocked you on the social list. There is only 1 reason to not show them.",
